## Best Practices

- Always use try/catch and WP.logMessage for error handling.
- Log all key actions and errors with logMessage().
- Validate elements with checkElement() before interaction.
- Use randomWait() to simulate human behavior.
- Support both XPath and CSS selectors.
- Always scroll before interacting with offscreen elements.
- Prefer smartScroll() over raw scrollPage().
- Combine scrolling with delays.
- Use ispScroll() in email interfaces.
- End scripts with WP.stopScript() if needed.
- Start script with WP.startScript() if needed.

---

## Frame Handling (iframes)

To interact with iframes, always get a reference to the correct frame.
Use the `frame` parameter when supported by functions like getText, clickElement, getAttribute, etc.
Wrap iframe interactions in try/catch.
